{"author":{"id":"60e8a4f6c4ac173f9427846756ea0ba4ba542d61e99b8bc2fc9c99440a92cf8c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795252398,"nonce":"BXIXRu3Ge+CN/YwMiFUJ7sg1OPU=","title":"Switch web from HTTP to Web Bluetooth and host it on GitHub Pages","message":"Config over Bluetooth replaces the Wi-Fi soft AP and captive portal. It needs no Wi-Fi, and the\nsame GATT service carries over if the firmware moves to the nRF52840. Web Bluetooth works in Chrome\nand Edge on Windows, macOS, ChromeOS and Android (Linux behind a flag), but not in Safari, Firefox or\nanything on iOS.\n\nSwitch `web` from HTTP (`gloo-net`) to Web Bluetooth, and host the built UI on GitHub Pages.","files":null}]}